// Step 2.1: GetVar(i, n) and SetVar(i, n, value) on a NOS 2 function.
// Arguments come first: a is var 0, b var 1, the local sum var 2. Setting
// sum to 100 changes what Calc prints and returns. Var 3 is out of range.
// FindVar needs named locals (an argFrame), which NOS 2 functions don't
// have, so it throws.
// Note: [(api:GetVar(...)), ...] needs the parentheses; [api:GetVar(...)]
// would be an array of class 'api holding a call to a global GetVar().
global Calc(a, b)
begin
  local sum := a + b;
  BreakLoop();
  Print([a, b, sum]);
  sum * 2;
end;

Print(Calc(3, 4));
